WEBVTT

NOTE understand-spatial-adjust: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.505
What the feature actually does:
turn the latest moisture scan into

V0-2
00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:10.190
today's percent adjustment, and
write it to Lynx when you push.

V1a-1
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.080
It lives inside IntelliDash. Access is
checked per user before the view loads.

V1b-1
00:00:17.636 --> 00:00:20.566
The Spatial Adjust header,
inside IntelliDash.

V2a-1
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:31.486
Each station's Avg. VWC comes
from a TurfRad moisture scan:

V2a-2
00:00:31.586 --> 00:00:35.890
the mean volumetric water content
measured across the station,

V2a-3
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:39.740
with the date it was captured
beside the station name.

V2b-1
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.890
Measured moisture and its
scan date, per station.

V3a-1
00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:53.423
Target VWC is the moisture
you want that station to hold.

V3a-2
00:00:53.523 --> 00:00:58.010
It is yours to set, station by
station, between 0 and 50 percent.

V3b-1
00:00:58.523 --> 00:01:03.228
The gap between measured and target
is what the calculation works on.

V3b-2
00:01:03.328 --> 00:01:06.533
Target VWC is an editable
input, not a reading.

V4a-1
00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:18.233
The difference between target and measured
moisture becomes an amount of water,

V4a-2
00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:21.018
today's ET is added,
the daily maximum caps it,

V4a-3
00:01:21.118 --> 00:01:25.460
and the result is divided by the Lynx
reference amount to give a percentage.

V4b-1
00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:28.840
The Suggested column is
the output of that chain.

V5a-1
00:01:34.613 --> 00:01:38.833
Spatial Adjust never waters anything.
Nothing changes until you push.

V5b-1
00:01:39.396 --> 00:01:42.416
Push Changes is the only thing
that writes to the controller.
